1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,950
If you want to deploy a cluster, start with Deploy a Cluster.

2
00:00:03,362 --> 00:00:05,400
You do not need to search through script names.

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:10,562
Start Here offers four choices: deploy, configure an existing cluster,

4
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:13,962
monitor and verify, or run saved automation.

5
00:00:14,362 --> 00:00:18,075
This series follows the current console with simulated examples.

6
00:00:18,488 --> 00:00:21,475
It does not execute changes against a real environment.

7
00:00:22,642 --> 00:00:24,742
Open Overview for the daily operations view.

8
00:00:25,142 --> 00:00:29,929
Its four main cards take you to deployment, configuration, infrastructure

9
00:00:29,942 --> 00:00:31,429
recovery, and monitoring.

10
00:00:31,829 --> 00:00:34,954
These are navigation links, not execution buttons.

11
00:00:35,367 --> 00:00:40,117
The summary below shows recorded cluster profiles, datacenters, running

12
00:00:40,117 --> 00:00:41,854
jobs and approvals.

13
00:00:42,267 --> 00:00:44,992
A profile count comes from saved recovery records.

14
00:00:45,404 --> 00:00:48,829
It is not an automatic discovery of every cluster.

15
00:00:50,017 --> 00:00:52,317
Read Needs attention before starting new work.

16
00:00:52,717 --> 00:00:57,229
A drift result, profile review warning, pending approval or failed

17
00:00:57,229 --> 00:00:59,504
job should take you to its detailed record.

18
00:00:59,917 --> 00:01:02,829
Check the target, timestamp and latest result there.

19
00:01:03,217 --> 00:01:06,617
A job marked succeeded means the execution completed.

20
00:01:07,029 --> 00:01:10,967
It does not mean that cluster health, requested settings or recovery

21
00:01:10,967 --> 00:01:13,067
readiness have been independently verified.

22
00:01:14,267 --> 00:01:17,379
Open Clusters to find saved recovery profiles.

23
00:01:17,817 --> 00:01:22,179
Filter by datacenter or cluster name, then open the matching profile.

24
00:01:22,579 --> 00:01:27,017
Check its captured baseline and review status before preparing recovery.

25
00:01:27,429 --> 00:01:31,117
Other cluster configuration files remain in Config Files.

26
00:01:31,517 --> 00:01:35,629
An empty profile list does not mean there are no physical clusters,

27
00:01:35,892 --> 00:01:39,142
and a listed profile does not prove its target is reachable.

28
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:44,138
The streamlined sidebar keeps ordinary tasks visible.

29
00:01:44,538 --> 00:01:49,612
Expand Advanced Automation for workflows, scripts, configuration files,

30
00:01:49,862 --> 00:01:52,125
schedules and execution history.

31
00:01:52,512 --> 00:01:56,338
Optional Integrations contains the preview integration paths.

32
00:01:56,725 --> 00:02:01,588
Administration contains setup, credentials, appliance operations and

33
00:02:01,588 --> 00:02:02,262
settings.

34
00:02:02,662 --> 00:02:07,088
N K P Validation Evidence carries a Preview badge and retains its

35
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:08,338
specialist sources.

36
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:13,925
Use execution history and target readbacks for ordinary cluster verification.

37
00:02:15,179 --> 00:02:20,054
For a normal task, choose the correct workflow, review the saved configuration,

38
00:02:20,542 --> 00:02:25,204
run the available dry run, obtain any required approval, and submit

39
00:02:25,204 --> 00:02:25,679
once.

40
00:02:26,179 --> 00:02:27,892
Follow its record in Jobs and Queue.

41
00:02:28,279 --> 00:02:30,717
Investigate failures before retrying.

42
00:02:31,117 --> 00:02:35,142
You can retain Start Here or Overview as your browser landing preference.

43
00:02:35,554 --> 00:02:39,629
Part two follows cluster deployment through the Foundation V M workflow.
